<urn:kbase:stmt/rex-9bc2b9b99c4f9317>
    rdf:type rdf:Statement ;
    rdf:subject kb:rx-what-to-check ;
    rdf:predicate rdfs:comment ;
    rdf:object "Demonstrates F223.9, F223.10 and F223.11 (a fact's standing, drawn by standing, and filtered by standing). Everything here is made up. 1) Look at the graph: held facts are solid; the two options of the greenhouse proposal are DASHED; the three questions end at hollow nodes marked \"?\". 2) In the view settings, open the legend: it should name held, proposed and question. 3) Switch the filter chips: \"Proposed\" should light only the dashed option edges, \"Questions\" only the three question ends; a held edge between two proposal nodes must stay quiet. 4) Add ?focus=option-a-north-lot to the address and reload: option A lights, option B dims; swap in option-b-courtyard and no node should move. 5) Weakness to know: nothing in the app stamps proposalOption on real facts yet, so \"proposed\" only appears on a seeded space like this one." ;
    meta:status "confirmed" ;
    meta:confidence "1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    meta:reviewMetadata "{\"version\":1,\"fields\":{\"sourceId\":\"review-example-proposals\",\"updatedAt\":1794301200000}}" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom src:review-example-proposals ;
    dc:created "2026-11-10T09:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

